----- stdout -----
core.memory.swappiness  Raise vm.swappiness for zram swap

  Why       When swap lives in zram, a swapped-out page is compressed into RAM
            rather than written to disk, so swapping early frees more usable
            memory at almost no cost. This raises swappiness to the value zram
            setups use, and only when zram is the swap the kernel fills first.

  Needs     your password, because it changes something outside your home
  Here      not applicable (swap is on disk, not zram; the default swappiness
            is right)

  Undo      gameready rollback
